        Root cause:
        The bug arises from the handling of the `alloc_dax()` function's return value. Specifically, the function was treating any error from `alloc_dax()` as a fatal error, which could lead to unnecessary failures in device allocation. The `-EOPNOTSUPP` error, indicating that the operation is not supported, was not being handled appropriately, causing the allocation process to terminate prematurely even when it could continue without DAX support.

        Commit message:
        dm: treat alloc_dax() -EOPNOTSUPP failure as non-fatal

In preparation for checking whether the architecture has data cache
aliasing within alloc_dax(), modify the error handling of dm alloc_dev()
to treat alloc_dax() -EOPNOTSUPP failure as non-fatal.

Link: https://lkml.kernel.org/r/20240215144633.96437-5-mathieu.desnoyers@efficios.com
Fixes: d92576f1167c ("dax: does not work correctly with virtual aliasing caches")
